---
title: Trojanized Electron/Node.js Crypto Application Execution
id: 8d1e2f3a-4b5c-4d7e-f6a7-9b0c1d2e3f01
status: experimental
description: Detects execution of an Electron/Node.js packaged application from a non-standard install path shortly after download, matching TraderTraitor's distribution of trojanized cryptocurrency trading or wallet applications.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.wiz.io/blog/north-korean-tradertraitor-crypto-heist
    - https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/cybersecurity-advisories/aa22-108a
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1566
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_electron:
        Image|endswith: '\electron.exe'
    selection_download_path:
        Image|contains:
            - '\Downloads\'
            - '\Temp\'
    condition: selection_electron and selection_download_path
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate Electron application installed directly from a download folder before relocation
level: medium

---
title: Recruiter-Themed PDF or Coding-Test Script Executed by Developer
id: 8d1e2f3a-4b5c-4d7e-f6a7-9b0c1d2e3f02
status: experimental
description: Detects a Python script or PDF reader spawning a child process shortly after opening a file with a job-offer or coding-test related name, matching TraderTraitor's LinkedIn recruiter lure delivery pattern.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.invictus-ir.com/news/profiling-tradetraitor-tactics-history-defenses
tags:
    - attack.initial_access
    - attack.t1566.001
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_lure_name:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\python.exe'
            - '\AcroRd32.exe'
    ParentCommandLine|contains:
        - 'coding_test'
        - 'coding-challenge'
        - 'job_offer'
        - 'interview_task'
    condition: selection_lure_name
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate internally-authored coding assessment named similarly
level: medium

---
title: New IAM User, Role, or Access Key Created Outside CI/CD Pipeline
id: 8d1e2f3a-4b5c-4d7e-f6a7-9b0c1d2e3f03
status: experimental
description: Detects creation of a new IAM user, role, or access key by a principal not associated with an approved automation/CI-CD identity, matching TraderTraitor's persistence technique observed in the Bybit intrusion.
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.sygnia.co/blog/sygnia-investigation-bybit-hack/
tags:
    - attack.persistence
    - attack.t1136.003
logsource:
    category: application
    service: aws_cloudtrail
detection:
    selection:
        eventName:
            - 'CreateUser'
            - 'CreateRole'
            - 'CreateAccessKey'
    filter_cicd:
        userIdentity.arn|contains: 'APPROVED_CICD_ROLE_LIST'  # populate with known automation role ARNs
    condition: selection and not filter_cicd
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate manual IAM provisioning by an authorized cloud admin outside automated pipelines
level: high

