---
title: Unauthorized Modification of Hosted Frontend Bundle in S3
id: 8d1e2f3a-4b5c-4d7e-f6a7-9b0c1d2e3f07
status: experimental
description: Detects a PutObject event modifying a production JavaScript bundle in an S3 bucket serving a live web frontend, outside of a recognized CI/CD deployment role, matching TraderTraitor's injection of malicious JavaScript to alter transaction payloads (as in the Bybit/Safe{Wallet} case).
author: Dalton Hunter
date: 2026/08/23
references:
    - https://www.elastic.co/security-labs/bit-bybit
tags:
    - attack.defense_evasion
    - attack.t1578.002
    - attack.impact
logsource:
    category: application
    service: aws_cloudtrail
detection:
    selection:
        eventName: 'PutObject'
        requestParameters.key|endswith: '.js'
        requestParameters.bucketName|contains: 'PRODUCTION_FRONTEND_BUCKET_LIST'  # populate with production hosting buckets
    filter_cicd:
        userIdentity.arn|contains: 'APPROVED_CICD_ROLE_LIST'  # populate with known automation role ARNs
    condition: selection and not filter_cicd
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate manual hotfix deployment by an authorized engineer outside the normal pipeline
level: critical

